system Auth  @app/api/auth/
  doc Handles user signup, login (credentials and Google OAuth), token refresh, password reset, and OTP verification requests.
  actor User
  part UserService, BillingService
  item VerificationOTP {otp_id, otp}
  item TokenPair {access_token, refresh_token}
  item Email
  item Password
  item Name
  item GoogleAccessToken
  item RefreshToken
  item OTPID
  item Purpose
  req AUTH-1 block an action (login, signup, password reset, send OTP) when the user's action rate or other constraints are exceeded  @credentials.go:26-35  ? how IsActionAllowed decides -> app/domains/user/
  req AUTH-2 verify a one-time password before signup or password reset; reject if invalid  @:74-77  ? how VerifyOTP works -> app/domains/user/
  usecase SignUp: User -> request verification OTP, verify OTP, provide email/name/password, receive token pair  @:61-85
  usecase LoginWithCredentials: User -> provide email and password, receive token pair  @:17-43
  usecase LoginWithGoogle: User -> provide Google access token, receive token pair  @:47-57
  usecase RefreshToken: User -> provide refresh token, receive new token pair  @:89-100
  usecase ResetPassword: User -> request verification OTP, verify OTP, provide new password, receive token pair  @password.go:17-50
  usecase RequestVerificationOTP: User -> provide email and purpose, receive OTP ID  @verification.go:17-55
  omit clientIP: implementation
  omit BearerToken: implementation
  omit DecodeJSONBody: implementation
  omit response.WriteError, response.JSON, response.Error: implementation
  omit httputil: implementation
  omit billingSvc: wiring
  ? how IsActionAllowed decides -> app/domains/user/
  ? how VerifyOTP works -> app/domains/user/
  ? how OAuthGoogleLogin works -> app/domains/user/
  ? how Refresh works -> app/domains/user/
  ? how SendOTP works -> app/domains/user/
  ? how SetPassword works -> app/domains/user/
  ? how GetUserByEmail works -> app/domains/user/
  ? how CreateLoginResponse works -> app/domains/user/
